  <revision rev="1" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>bd462f6ccfcb0a86db0e5192181ee5df</srcmd5>
    <version>1.46.0</version>
    <time>1787063810</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>goose 1.46.0 - re-adding the package that was removed in sr#1349940

This is a NEW-package submission for a package Factory used to have. goose
shipped in Factory from November 2025 until 2026-04-29, when kskarthik asked
for it to be removed in sr#1349940: &quot;I'm having build issues with recent
versions &amp; it might take some more time to resolve it. Meanwhile, it is not
ideal to have old version in factory.&quot;

That build problem is fixed, and the fix is small. The spec already built with
--no-default-features, but the only feature it then asked for was
disable-update - and disable-update is a goose-cli-only feature, so nothing
turned a TLS backend back on. reqwest was therefore compiled without one and
the build died with seven rustc errors about reqwest::Certificate and
reqwest::Identity not existing. The fix is to name the features to KEEP rather
than the one to add: the spec now builds

  --no-default-features --features aws-providers,nostr,otel,rustls-tls,
                                   system-keyring,tui,disable-update

which restores the TLS backend and the provider set while still leaving out
code-mode (whose vendored v8 crate downloads a prebuilt V8 at build time, which
an offline distribution build cannot do), local inference and telemetry.

kskarthik is still the maintainer of goose in science:machinelearning:mcp and
accepted this work into the devel project himself earlier today, as sr#1371447;
I was added as co-maintainer at the same time. The package's Factory history is
his - nine accepted submissions between sr#1317774 and sr#1331145 - and this
submission builds directly on it.

What else is in the package, beyond the version bump to 1.46.0:

- License: re-derived from the vendored crate graph rather than inherited. The
  binary statically links its dependencies, so the tag covers the whole linked
  set: 13 SPDX identifiers, read from the &quot;license =&quot; field of every crate in
  the 608-crate linked graph (1235 are vendored; the code-mode and local-
  inference branches are not built, so v8/candle/llama-cpp are not in it). The
  derivation, and why each non-permissive identifier is there, is written out
  as a Legal-Review-Notice above the tag. The MPL-2.0 and LGPL-3.0 source
  requirements are met by vendor-crates.tar.zst shipping in the src.rpm, and
  both texts are installed as %license files.
- goose-system-libdbus.patch links the system libdbus instead of the copy
  bundled in libdbus-sys. Downstream-only on purpose: upstream needs the
  vendored build for its portable/musl binaries.
- 45 man pages, generated by upstream's own generator binary walking the same
  clap tree the CLI uses.
- bash/fish/zsh completion subpackages, generated from the clap definitions.
- %check exercises the produced binary (--version, info, and an assertion that
  the &quot;update&quot; subcommand really is compiled out) rather than the workspace
  test suite, which drives live provider back ends and needs vendor API keys.

Built locally for 16.1/aarch64; OBS has it green on openSUSE_Tumbleweed,
development, 16.0 and 16.1 at the submitted revision. The devel project's
SLE_15_SP7 repo is red, but it was red on the previous version too - its cargo
is too old to read the lock file - and it is not a Factory target.</comment>
